Commit:     Brendan Abolivier <brendan@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Thu Jul 3 09:35:54 2025 -0700

    Bug 1971540 - Part 1: Remove nsIMsgMailSession's and nsIMsgUserFeedbackListener's dependency on nsIMsgMailNewsUrl. r=darktrojan


    EWS will need the ability to use the `nsIMsgMailSession::Alert*` methods to
    properly propagate authentication and security errors to the user. Since EWS
    URLs aren't derived from `nsIMsgMailNewsUrl`, we need to make
    `nsIMsgMailSession` and `nsIMsgUserFeedbackListener` support "plain" `nsIURI`s
    (we could technically use `nsIURL`, but we don't use anything from there that
    isn't inherited from `nsIURI`).

    From a look at the (only) implementation of both interfaces, it seems like we
    only use the mailnews-specific bits of the URLs to retrieve the message window,
    and use its presence to figure out whether we should alert the user. I've
    slightly altered this behaviour by requiring all consumers to figure out whether
    the alert should be silent by themselves.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D253342

